Enable dma-buf (DRM PRIME) paths on illumos as on Linux and the BSDs.

The illumos DRM core (virtio_gpu) reports DRM_CAP_PRIME; without the cap
Mesa offers no EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import or GBM fd import (so Xorg glamor
has no DRI3), and anv/venus need vk_image::drm_format_mod.  Upstreamable.

--- src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c.orig
+++ src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@
 
    caps->throttle = true;
 
-#if defined(HAVE_LIBDRM) && (DETECT_OS_LINUX || DETECT_OS_BSD || DETECT_OS_MANAGARM)
+#if defined(HAVE_LIBDRM) && (DETECT_OS_LINUX || DETECT_OS_BSD || DETECT_OS_MANAGARM || DETECT_OS_SOLARIS)
    if (pscreen->get_screen_fd) {
       uint64_t cap;
       int fd = pscreen->get_screen_fd(pscreen);
